From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Subject: [PATCH] MIPS: treat every Config4.IE value above 1 as TLBINV

decode_config4() sets MIPS_CPU_TLBINV only for IE == 2. The XBurst2 core
that QEMU's ingenic-t41 machine models ("XBurst2-MXU3.1", PRID
0x00132100) reports IE == 3 in Config4, and QEMU implements TLBINV,
TLBINVF and EntryHi.EHINV for every IE >= 2.

With TLBINV unset the kernel takes the legacy branch of
r4k_tlb_configure() and calls r4k_tlb_uniquify(), which rewrites every
TLB entry with a 4 KiB PageMask, FTLB indices included. QEMU's FTLB
write check rejects an entry whose PageMask or set does not match the
FTLB geometry with a machine check, so the first tlbwi in
r4k_tlb_uniquify_write() raises ExcCode 24 before trap_init() has
installed a vector, and the guest loops in the exception handler.

The kernel already assumes an FTLB machine has TLBINV - tlbex.c has
BUG_ON(!cpu_has_tlbinv) on the FTLB flush path - so accept the range.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
--- a/arch/mips/kernel/cpu-probe.c
+++ b/arch/mips/kernel/cpu-probe.c
@@ -569,7 +569,13 @@
 	config4 = read_c0_config4();
 
 	if (cpu_has_tlb) {
-		if (((config4 & MIPS_CONF4_IE) >> 29) == 2)
+		/*
+		 * IE 1 adds TLBINV/TLBINVF, IE 2 adds EntryHi.EHINV on top of
+		 * them and IE 3 is the whole set again. Anything above 1 has
+		 * the invalidation instructions, so accept the range instead
+		 * of the single value mainline names.
+		 */
+		if (((config4 & MIPS_CONF4_IE) >> 29) >= 2)
 			c->options |= MIPS_CPU_TLBINV;
 
 		/*
